			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				989,
				16
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Decompose Window RPC handlers into file-per-struct modules\n\nExtract all gRPC entry points within the `Source/RPC/CocoonService/Window` namespace into dedicated PascalCase modules. This completes the architectural refactor initiated in previous commits for Workspace, Command, and Configuration, ensuring the monolithic `mod.rs` no longer contains inline handler logic.\n\nNew modules include handlers for window management (CreateWebviewPanel, DisposeWebviewPanel, SetWebviewHtml), status bar operations (CreateStatusBarItem, SetStatusBarText), and user interface interactions (ShowErrorMessage, ShowInformationMessage, ShowWarningMessage, ShowInputBox, ShowQuickPick, ShowTextDocument). Additional handlers cover progress reporting (ShowProgress, ReportProgress) and webview messaging (OnDidReceiveMessage, PostWebviewMessage).\n\nEach handler implements the `Fn` signature required by Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro and bridges the `Vine` gRPC protocol to the `Sky` UI layer. The implementations utilize the `CommonLibrary` traits (`StatusBarProvider`, `WebviewProvider`, `UserInterfaceProvider`) for state registration and stateful operations. Fallback mechanisms via direct `sky://` Tauri events are preserved for trait failures to prevent state leaks in webview and status bar components.",
			"SHA": "adfab9f41833191c1652fc00fb0b0d91aa16054d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:37:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				972,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose Workspace RPC handlers into file-per-struct modules\n\nDecompose the `Source/RPC/CocoonService/Workspace` module to align with the project-wide PascalCase file-per-struct convention. Extract the handler logic for `ApplyEdit`, `OpenDocument`, `SaveAll`, `UpdateConfiguration`, and `UpdateWorkspaceFolders` into dedicated submodules.\n\nEach handler is exposed as a public async function `Fn` within its own file, invoked via fully qualified paths in the parent `mod.rs`. The implementations bridge the gRPC `Vine` protocol to the frontend: `ApplyEdit`, `OpenDocument`, `SaveAll`, and `UpdateConfiguration` emit specific Tauri events to the `Sky` UI layer, while `UpdateWorkspaceFolders` performs direct mutation of the `ApplicationState.Workspace` DTOs and triggers the standard notification mechanism. This preserves all existing logic for text editing ranges, untitled file handling, and folder index stability, ensuring consistent symbol resolution for Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro.",
			"SHA": "3ad7df3dc9d9447ced7b2baf5725e63fb4752381"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:37:15Z",
